<main><section id="explore"><div class="intro"><div><div class="eyebrow"><span class="red-line"></span> DANCING WITH THE SARS</div><h1>A changing planet.<br>A clearer perspective.</h1><p>Compare Earth observations. Investigate surface change.<br>Turn satellite measurements into evidence you can explore.</p><a class="text-link" href="#workspace">Explore the observations <span>↓</span></a></div><div class="mission"><span class="eyebrow">MISSION BRIEF / 01</span><h3>Observe.<br>Compare.<br>Understand.</h3><p>NASA imagery and NISAR discovery.<br>One workspace. Traceable sources.</p></div></div>
<div class="kpis" aria-label="Latest radar analysis statistics"><article><span>Total Areas Analyzed</span><strong id="kpiAreas">0</strong><small>Unique uploaded datasets this session</small></article><article><span>Change Percentage</span><strong id="kpiChange">—</strong><small id="kpiChangeNote">Run a radar analysis to measure change</small></article><article><span>Confidence Score</span><strong class="unavailable">Not assessed</strong><small>Independent validation required</small></article><article><span>Observation Date</span><strong id="kpiDate" class="date">—</strong><small id="kpiDateNote">Latest analyzed SAR acquisition</small></article></div>
<div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">01 / VISUAL OBSERVATIONS</span><h2>Two moments. One landscape.</h2></div><span class="status-dot">NASA GIBS · Optical imagery</span></div>
<div class="workspace" id="workspace"><aside><h3>Observation settings</h3><label>Study region<select id="region"><option value="24.7,46.7,7">Riyadh, Saudi Arabia</option><option value="45,59,6">Aral Sea, Central Asia</option><option value="-10,-55,6">Amazon Basin, Brazil</option><option value="30.7,32.3,7">Nile Delta, Egypt</option></select></label><label>Before<input id="before" type="date" value="2020-06-15"></label><label>After<input id="after" type="date" value="2025-06-15"></label><button id="compare" class="primary">Update comparison <span>→</span></button><p class="hint">Pan or zoom either map. Both views stay synchronized.</p><p id="status" role="status"></p><hr><button id="search">Find NISAR observations ↗</button><button id="export" class="quiet">Export observation report ↓</button></aside><div class="comparison"><div class="map-pair"><div class="map-wrap"><div class="map-caption"><b>BEFORE</b><time id="beforeLabel"></time></div><div id="map" class="map" aria-label="Before satellite observation"></div></div><div class="map-wrap"><div class="map-caption"><b>AFTER</b><time id="afterLabel"></time></div><div id="mapAfter" class="map" aria-label="After satellite observation"></div></div></div><div class="caption">TERRA / MODIS TRUE COLOR <span>Optical context · Clouds and seasonal conditions affect interpretation</span></div></div></div>
<div class="results"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">02 / RADAR DISCOVERY</span><h2>NISAR observation catalog</h2></div><span class="mono">NASA CMR / GCOV</span></div><p id="catalogStatus" role="status">Search the current map extent to retrieve available satellite observations.</p><div id="catalog"></div></div>
<div class="workflow"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">FROM ACQUISITION TO INSIGHT</span><h2>The analysis workflow</h2></div></div><ol><li><span>01</span><h3>NISAR data</h3><p>Discover GCOV observations.</p><small>Connected catalog</small></li><li><span>02</span><h3>Preprocessing</h3><p>Calibrate, align and quality-check.</p><small>External preparation</small></li><li><span>03</span><h3>Change detection</h3><p>Measure backscatter differences.</p><small>Available in radar analysis</small></li><li><span>04</span><h3>Interpretation</h3><p>Read an automatic evidence summary.</p><small>Rule-based · AI model not connected</small></li><li><span>05</span><h3>Interactive dashboard</h3><p>Inspect and export the findings.</p><small>Available</small></li></ol></div>
<div class="impact"><span class="eyebrow">THE CHALLENGE / REAL-WORLD VALUE</span><h2>How can this help?</h2><p class="impact-intro">Make surface change easier to investigate, explain and act on.</p><div class="impact-grid"><article><span>01 / CITIES</span><h3>Monitor urban expansion</h3><p>Compare observations around growing cities and identify where closer analysis is needed.</p></article><article><span>02 / ENVIRONMENT</span><h3>Track environmental change</h3><p>Explore changes around water bodies, agricultural landscapes and forest regions.</p></article><article><span>03 / DECISIONS</span><h3>Support research</h3><p>Keep dates, sources and analysis methods attached to exported evidence.</p></article><article><span>04 / ACCESS</span><h3>Make SAR understandable</h3><p>Translate backscatter measurements into clear comparisons, with uncertainty visible.</p></article></div><p class="hint">These are intended applications. Confirming land-cover classes requires additional data and validation.</p></div></section>
<section id="radar" hidden><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">ANALYSIS WORKSPACE</span><h1>Read the radar signal.</h1><p>Compare two aligned, calibrated backscatter grids. Inspect the change before drawing conclusions.</p></div></div><div class="lab"><aside><h3>Input data</h3><label>Paired raster grids · JSON<input type="file" id="upload" accept=".json"></label><button id="schema">Download input template ↓</button><label>Change threshold · dB<input type="number" id="threshold" value="3" min="0.1" max="30" step="0.1"></label><button id="analyze" class="primary">Run change detection →</button><p id="labStatus" role="status">Upload a dataset to begin. The input template contains synthetic example values only.</p><button id="report" disabled>Export analysis report ↓</button></aside><article class="analysis-body"><div class="analysis-empty" id="emptyState"><span class="crosshair">⊕</span><h3>Awaiting observations</h3><p>Your change map will appear here after analysis.</p></div><canvas id="change" width="700" height="350" hidden aria-label="Radar backscatter change map"></canvas><div class="legend"><span><i class="orange"></i>Increased backscatter</span><span><i class="blue"></i>Decreased backscatter</span><span><i class="gray"></i>Below threshold</span><span>Black: no data</span></div><div id="metrics" class="metrics"></div><div class="summary"><span class="eyebrow">ANALYSIS SUMMARY</span><h3 id="summaryTitle">Evidence first. Interpretation second.</h3><p id="summaryText" role="status">Run an analysis to generate a plain-language summary of the measured change.</p><small>Automatically generated from measured statistics using explicit rules. No AI model or confidence estimate is applied.</small></div><details><summary>How to interpret backscatter change</summary><p>Increased backscatter may reflect buildings, surface roughness or moisture. Decreases may relate to calm water, moisture changes or vegetation disturbance. A two-date difference alone does not establish urban expansion or land-cover class.</p><p>Use the same sensor, polarization and orbit, with calibrated, terrain-corrected, speckle-treated and co-registered data. Direct NISAR / RADARSAT-1 differencing is not supported.</p></details></article></div></section>
<section id="sources" hidden><span class="eyebrow">PROVENANCE & METHODS</span><h1>Every observation<br>has a source.</h1><div class="cards"><article><span class="eyebrow">RADAR / DISCOVERY</span><h2>NASA–ISRO NISAR</h2><p>Live GCOV discovery through NASA CMR. Scientific downloads require Earthdata Login on the official service. Credentials are never collected here.</p><a href="https://nisar-docs.asf.alaska.edu/earthaccess/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Access documentation ↗</a></article><article><span class="eyebrow">OPTICAL / MAPS</span><h2>NASA GIBS</h2><p>Daily Terra MODIS true-color imagery. Used as visual context, not as radar data or a measurement of urban area.</p><a href="https://nasa-gibs.github.io/gibs-api-docs/access-basics/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Imagery service ↗</a></article><article><span class="eyebrow">RADAR / ARCHIVE</span><h2>RADARSAT-1</h2><p>Historical Canadian SAR imagery in an open AWS COG archive. External access only; archive ingestion is not integrated.</p><a href="https://registry.opendata.aws/radarsat-1/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">AWS dataset ↗</a> · <a href="https://github.com/asc-csa/radarsat1-scripts" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CSA scripts ↗</a></article><article><span class="eyebrow">CANADIAN DATA SERVICES</span><h2>EODMS / CSA</h2><p>Canadian Earth observation discovery services. Availability of individual records depends on the upstream provider.</p><a href="https://www.eodms-sgdot.nrcan-rncan.gc.ca/index-en.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">EODMS ↗</a> · <a href="https://donnees-data.asc-csa.gc.ca/en/dataset/radarsat1" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CSA dataset ↗</a></article></div><h2>Measurement, not a classification claim</h2><p>The lab computes after minus before in dB and counts valid pixels whose absolute difference meets the selected threshold. Missing pixels are excluded. Change percentage is not an accuracy score or a land-cover estimate.</p><p>Areas analyzed counts unique non-demo uploaded datasets with valid results in this browser session. Re-running a threshold does not add another area. Observation date refers to the latest analyzed SAR pair, not the optical map dates. Confidence remains unassessed until independent validation exists.</p><h2>Development status</h2><p>No raw HDF5/GeoTIFF preprocessing, validated urban/vegetation/water classification, cross-sensor harmonization or AI service is connected. Preprocessed raster grids are supplied by the user. Synthetic inputs are explicitly labeled and excluded from the area count.</p></section></main>
